      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=#Role \nYour job is to classify the incoming message into *intents* and then create a json configuration as mentioned below\n\n#Rules\n- Do not make up the intents \n- Strictly adhere to the output \n- do not add newline character\n- based on the received text, categorizer the text into one of below intents i) set_event 2)do_research 3)exec_action 4)rag_search where a) set_event - user is requesting to set an event, reminder, call, appointment, meeting b)do-research - user is requesting to perform a research on the stated topic c)exec_action is a specific action e.g. summarize towards meetings, events, entire day etc, requested by the user\nd)rag_search is an explicit request from user to use RAG or 'file' search later downstream to find the answer. \n- for set_event intent the *context* should inlcude the exact date if it mentioned in vague terms. E.g. Set meeting for tomorrow then return the exact date based on today . if time frame is not mentioned assume 00:00:00 but for cst timezone. For start_time and end_time use the format used in google calendar.\n- for exec_action intent use the provided *Table structure* to generate a sql query based on the user request and applicable table schema\n\n#Input\n##Message\n{{ $json.message }}\n\n#Output schema sample\na)if intent is set_event\n{\n  \"intent\": \"set_event\",\n  \"details\": {\n    \"user_message\":<the user message>\n    \"context\": {\n      \"event_name\": <name of the event>,\n      \"event_time\": {\n          \"start_time\":<start_time>\n          \"end_time\":<end_time>  \n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nb)if intent is do_research\n{\n  \"intent\": \"do_research\",\n  \"details\": {\n    \"user_message\":<the user message>,\n    \"context\": {\n      \"research_details\":<add instructions on how to do research>\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nc)if intent is exec_action\n{\n  \"intent\": \"exec_action\",\n  \"details\": {\n    \"user_message\":<the user message>,\n    \"context\": {\n      \"sql query\":<additional details as applicable>\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nc)if intent is rag_search \n{\n  \"intent\": \"rag_search\",\n  \"details\": {\n    \"user_message\":<the user message>,\n    \"context\": {\n      \"details\":<additional details as applicable>\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n\n#Table structure\n-table_name: agent_output\n-table_schema:  public.agent_output (\n  id bigint generated by default as identity not null,\n  created_at timestamp with time zone not null default now(),\n  agent_name text null,\n  agent_response json null,\n  status text null,\n  user_id text null,\n  constraint agent_output_pkey primary key (id)\n) TABLESPACE pg_default;\n- key column details\n  a) agent_name - one of calendar_agent, event_agent, ainews_agent, research_agent, investment_agent, expense_agent \nb) status - success, fail-nodata\n\n\n\n#Examples\n###input1\n-message - Set a reminder to call Mani next tuesday\n-output\n{\n  \"intent\": \"set_event\",\n  \"details\": {\n    \"user_message\":\"Set a reminder to call Mani next tuesday from 10 to 11 am\",\n    \"context\": {\n      \"event_name\": \"Reminder\",\n      \"event_time\": {\n          \"start_time\":2025-11-18T10:00:00.000-00:00\n          \"end_time\":2025-11-19T11:00:00.000-00:00\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n###input2\n-message - Perform research latest developments in quantum physics\n-output\n{\n  \"intent\": \"do_research\",\n  \"details\": {\n    \"user_message\":\"Perform research latest developments in quantum physics\",\n    \"context\": {\n      \"research_details\":\"\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n\n\n###input3\n-message - Summarize my day today\n-output\n{\n  \"intent\": \"exec_action\",\n  \"details\": {\n    \"user_message\":\"Summarize the ai news todays\",\n    \"context\": {\n      \"sql query\":\"SELECT agent_response from agent_output where agent_name = 'ainews_agent' and status = 'success' order by created_at  desc  limit 1\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n###input4\n-message - Control use RAG to find out which frameworks, LLM's support RAG natively\n-output\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"rag_search\",\n  \"details\": {\n    \"user_message\":\"Control use RAG to find out which frameworks, LLM's support RAG natively\",\n    \"context\": {\n      \"details\":\"\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n",
        "options": {}
      },
